The higher your alignment and the higher your luck, the better your
results will be.  You'll also have better results if you're standing
on a co-aligned altar.  (The 'Tyr is pleased' message suggests your
alignment is good enough for fixing trouble.)

Carrying a cursed loadstone is a minor problem from your god's point
of view, so Tyr's going to have to be pretty impressed to fix it.  If
you're going to get this fixed by prayer, you're going to need to have
decent luck, and (especially if luck is on the lower end) it'll help
to be standing on an altar.  (You need to get at least a 3 on a
d(luck) with a bonus of 3 for an altar and another 2 for a co-aligned
priest in attendance)

